{% doc %}
  Product card for collection/search grids: image tile at the global card
  ratio, then the text block — name + price on one line, the short subtitle
  under it, and the colour swatches under that (they took over the slot that
  used to be reserved empty for a selector).

  The grid's own gap is tight so the images sit close together; the air the
  text needs is inside the card instead (see .product-card__info in base.css),
  which is why the two are tuned separately.

  @param {product} product - the product to render
  @param {boolean} [featured] - oversized lead tile (spans 2×2 grid cells on
    desktop); also loads its image eagerly
  @param {boolean} [show_price] - defaults to true
  @param {boolean} [show_collection] - render the product's first collection
    title under the name (11px caps, muted); defaults to false
  @example
  {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, featured: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign price_visible = true
  if show_price == false
    assign price_visible = false
  endif

  comment
    Card widths written out rather than approximated with one vw figure — see
    the long note in main-product.liquid. Same reason: the left gutter is
    clamped, so the share of the viewport a card occupies changes with it, and
    an understated `sizes` is exactly what serves a too-small file.

    Four columns of (content - 3 gaps), where content = 100vw - gutter - 40:
      >= 1604px : (100vw - 340 - 30) / 4
      >=  990px : (81.3vw - 40 - 30) / 4
      750-989px : the grid drops to TWO columns
      <   750px : one column, full width less the page margins
    The featured tile spans two of those columns plus the gap between them.
  endcomment
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1604px) calc(25vw - 90px), (min-width: 990px) calc(20.3vw - 17px), (min-width: 750px) calc(40.6vw - 25px), calc(100vw - 80px)'
  assign card_sizes_featured = '(min-width: 1604px) calc(50vw - 175px), (min-width: 990px) calc(40.6vw - 25px), (min-width: 750px) calc(81.3vw - 40px), calc(100vw - 80px)'
-%}

<article class="product-card{% if featured %} product-card--featured{% endif %}" data-product-card>
  <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="product-card__link" data-card-link>
    <div class="product-card__media">
      {%- if product.featured_media -%}
        {%- if featured -%}
          {{-
            product.featured_media
            | image_url: width: 2000
            | image_tag:
              widths: '550, 750, 1100, 1500, 2000',
              sizes: card_sizes_featured,
              loading: 'eager',
              fetchpriority: 'high',
              class: 'product-card__image'
          -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{-
            product.featured_media
            | image_url: width: 1600
            | image_tag:
              widths: '360, 540, 720, 900, 1200, 1600',
              sizes: card_sizes,
              loading: 'lazy',
              class: 'product-card__image'
          -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="product-card__media--placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Name, subtitle and category stack on the left; price and compare-at sit
      opposite them on ONE line. Both come from the shown variant rather than
      the product, because compare-at can differ per colour — theme.js swaps
      the pair when a swatch is picked. The swatches themselves are links and
      so live outside this one, below the category.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign shown = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
    <div class="product-card__info">
      <div class="product-card__row">
        <div class="product-card__text">
          <h3 class="product-card__title">{{ product.title }}</h3>

          {% render 'product-subtitle', product: product, class: 'product-card__subtitle' %}

          {%- if show_collection -%}
            {%- capture card_category %}{% render 'product-category', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
            {%- if card_category != blank -%}
              <p class="product-card__collection">{{ card_category }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if price_visible -%}
          <p class="product-card__prices">
            <span class="product-card__price" data-card-price>{{ shown.price | money }}</span>
            {%- if shown.compare_at_price > shown.price -%}
              <s class="product-card__compare" data-card-compare>{{ shown.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
            {%- else -%}
              <s class="product-card__compare" data-card-compare hidden></s>
            {%- endif -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>

  {% render 'color-swatches', product: product, context: 'card' %}
</article>
